QSV can only map fixed-size D3D11 frame pools ("Only fixed-size pools can be mapped to QSV
frames"), and ddagrab allocates a dynamic pool. Honor the generic extra_hw_frames filter
option by fixing the pool at 8 plus that many frames, so Intel capture can run
ddagrab=...:extra_hw_frames=N,hwmap=derive_device=qsv without a CPU copy. Without the
option (the default -1) the pool stays dynamic, so NVENC, AMF and Media Foundation capture
are unchanged.

--- a/libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c
@@ -771,6 +771,8 @@ static av_cold int init_hwframes_ctx(AVFilterContext *avctx)
     dda->frames_ctx->format    = AV_PIX_FMT_D3D11;
     dda->frames_ctx->width     = dda->width;
     dda->frames_ctx->height    = dda->height;
+    if (avctx->extra_hw_frames > 0)
+        dda->frames_ctx->initial_pool_size = 8 + avctx->extra_hw_frames;

     switch (dda->raw_format) {
     case DXGI_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM:
